course: dictionary
lesson: 8760
title: Seventieth and other order words
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Seventieth is an ordinal number. It tells you position, which one comes in order: first, second, third, and so on up to seventieth. It means number 70 in the line, coming straight after the sixty-ninth. So «her seventieth birthday» is the birthday that comes after her sixty-ninth.
explain: Seventieth can also be a fraction. A seventieth is one of 70 equal parts of something, written 1/70. Look for clues: the word «a» or «one» in front of it, and the idea of sharing something out into equal parts. In «at 70 it is only one seventieth», the year is a tiny slice of a whole life.
explain: When you meet an order word, ask: is this about position in a line, or about one part of a whole? Then check by swapping in another word. If «seventieth» can become «seventh» or «70th» and still make sense in a list, it is about position.
fact: Seventieth means number 70 in order, so it is the 70th.
fact: The short form is 70th: the «th» shows it is an ordinal number.
fact: A seventieth is one of 70 equal parts of something, written 1/70.
fact: «Seventieth birthday» means a big celebration for grandparents who have reached 70 years old.
fact: Ordinal numbers show position: first, second, third, and so on, up to seventieth and beyond.
exercise: «She celebrated her seventieth birthday with a big cake.» What does seventieth mean here? | The last one ever | *The 70th in order | The seventh one | Seventy coins
exercise: Which is the short form of seventieth? | 17th | 7th | 700th | *70th
exercise: In «at 70 it is only one seventieth», what is a seventieth? | A number shown as 70 | *One of 70 equal parts | The 70th birthday party | Seventy years in a row
test: «The seventieth anniversary of the school was in May.» What does seventieth mean? | *The 70th in order | The seventh anniversary | A party with seventy guests | One of seventy equal parts
test: Which number comes just before the seventieth? | Seventy-first | Seventh | Seventieth again | *Sixty-ninth
exam: A seventieth is what fraction of a whole? | 70/1 | *1/70 | 7/10 | 1/7
